The bug occurs because `skb_pull()` can fail even when `pskb_inet_may_pull()` returns true. This situation arises when applications create malformed packets, such as those lacking an IP header. As a result, calling `skb_pull()` can lead to accessing uninitialized memory, causing undefined behavior.

